by nicolas-grekas at 2026-07-27T04:34:45Z

Updated: the scope is now derived from the URIs rather than hand-written, which is what @nicolas-grekas suggested back in August 2024.

The previous revision required an explicit `scope` alongside `base_uris`, because the regexp `forBaseUri()` derives from a single URI stops matching once the host rotates, and the scoped options would silently stop applying on the fallback host. Requiring the regexp was the conservative half of the answer; deriving it is the right one, and it also keeps the two from drifting apart when someone adds a URI to the list.

That needs a factory in the component rather than a `preg_quote` in the extension. The derivation is `resolveUrl(parseUrl("."), parseUrl($baseUri))`, which resolves `.` against the base and therefore drops the last path segment, and both helpers are private to `HttpClientTrait`. A naive version is wrong for any base URI carrying a path, and does not even match the base URI itself:

```
https://a.example.com/v1/api   derived: https\://a\.example\.com/v1/
                                naive: https\://a\.example\.com/v1/api/
```

So `ScopingHttpClient::forBaseUris()` joins the derived prefixes with `|`, uses the first URI as the default `base_uri`, and is covered by three unit tests in the component, including one asserting that an unlisted host is out of scope.

The config semantics shifted with it. `base_uris` now lists the URIs to fall back to **after** `base_uri`, instead of being the complete rotation list, so the primary host is no longer written twice. The effective list is `[base_uri, ...base_uris]` and both the scoping and the retryable client are given that same union. The `scope`-is-required rule is gone; a `base_uri` is required instead, which the scoped client config already effectively demanded.

The functional test now also proves the scope part, which is the bit the earlier revision got silently wrong:

```
GET https://a.example.com/posts/1 X-Scoped: yes
GET https://b.example.com/posts/1 X-Scoped: yes
```

With `forBaseUri()` in place of `forBaseUris()`, the header disappears from the second line while the rotation still happens.

FrameworkBundle now requires HttpClient 8.2 for the new factory, added as a `conflict` entry since http-client is a require-dev here, matching the `symfony/workflow` precedent in the same block.

Container for an existing `retry_failed` configuration is still byte identical, re-checked after these changes. Local runs: ScopingHttpClient 11, FrameworkBundle DI 514, functional HttpClient 5, all green.

